    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Meredith-Hall/Assistant-Professor-of-Sports-Media-and-Communication_JR100033": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sports Media and Communication",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Journalism and Mass Communications ‌ Department Summary: Drake University is a forward-thinking community of scholars with a focus on active, collaborative learning and applied scholarship. Drake is in Des Moines, Iowa—a vibrant city that is nationally recognized for its quality of life and a wealth of opportunities for professional, social and civic engagement. A Drake education couples hands-on training in professional skills with a strong liberal arts education. We strive to create a community of scholars that represents the complexity of the human experience in regards to race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, economic status, gender identification, religion, age and physical abilities. We are committed to creating a welcoming and supportive environment for all our faculty, staff, students and visitors. We develop and offer innovative programming serving a variety of audiences, including high school, undergraduate, and graduate students, as well as community members, industry professionals, and retirees. The successful applicant will join a collegial, welcoming, energetic and supportive community. Visit our website (drake.edu/sjmc) to learn more. Job Summary: The Drake School of Journalism and Mass Communication invites applications for a nine-month, consecutive term appointment of an assistant professor of sports media and communication, beginning in fall semester 2027.  Drake’s School of Journalism and Mass Communication is accredited by ACEJMC and offers seven award-winning undergraduate majors: advertising, content strategy and publishing, digital media production, multimedia journalism, public relations, sports media and communication, and strategic political communication. The School also has a successful online Master of Arts in Communication with tracks in brand communication, communication leadership, and public policy and advocacy. The successful applicant will join a collegial, welcoming and supportive community of 14 full-time faculty and staff, and approximately 350 undergraduate and graduate students. We are looking for an innovative colleague who embraces cutting-edge technologies and who can help lead our School in preparing our students for the rapidly changing media landscape.   Professional experience working in sports media is required. Ideally the candidate will have experience in sports production and live broadcasts. Candidates may also bring front-of-camera experience to the role. A portfolio of work is expected. Evidence of teaching effectiveness is preferred. Master’s degree is preferred, but we are open to hiring an experienced professional with a bachelor’s degree for this consecutive-term appointment. Qualified candidates will have a demonstrated ability to train and mentor students and a history of early adoption of new technologies. The ability to work with colleagues across disciplines to lead students in conceiving, creating, delivering, and promoting rich multimedia content packages for all platforms, and for all types of media outlets, is essential. Depending on skills and interest, teaching assignments may include these undergraduate courses, both on campus and online: Sports Writing, Sports Production, Reporting and Writing Principles, Multimedia Lab, Multimedia Sound Design, Electronic Field Production, Reporting for Television and the Web, and special topics courses focused on interactive reality, data visualization, and emerging technologies. The qualified candidate may also teach online graduate classes in Digital Media Strategies, Emerging Media, and Multimedia Storytelling. Course load is seven courses (4/3) over the academic year. Duties also include academic and career mentoring for students, advising a student media organization or student sports production, and service to the University and community. The search committee is particularly interested in candidates who, through their teaching, scholarship/creative activity, and service, will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. Minimum Qualifications: ● An advanced degree (MA, MS) in Communication, Media, Journalism or a related field or equivalent professional experience, which SJMC defines as “at least three to five years of broad and deep experience in real-world situations relevant to the discipline in which the faculty member would be teaching.” ● Potential for successful teaching of undergraduate courses in sports media production ● Production experience directly related to sports media, media production, television production, news production or related fields ● Record of professional achievement related to sports media production ● Excellent written communication skills ● Expressed desire to provide equal opportunity for all students    Preferred Qualifications: While not everyone may meet all preferred qualifications, the ideal candidate will bring many of the following: ● Experience teaching at the college or university level ● Successful experience in the following: - working collaboratively with others (e.g., committee service, being part of a production team, co-teaching); - working independently (e.g., supervising a production, course development) ● Experience in Live Sports Productions as any of the following: - Producer - Director - Technical Director - Replay Operator - Audio Operator - Camera Operator - Graphics Operator - Talent (Play-By-Play/Analyst) ● Experience in Sports Newsrooms/Departments as any of the following: - Anchor - Reporter (MMJ) - Videographer - Editor - Producer - Director ● Demonstrated successful experience teaching undergraduate media production courses ● Experience connecting and collaborating with media industry professionals on the local, regional, and/or national levels ● Effective interpersonal communication skills ● Effective oral communication skills ● Effective classroom management skills ● Expressed commitment to Drake University’s mission and values. ● Terminal degree in communication, media or related field (MFA, PhD) ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete the online application and attach (1) a letter of interest, (2) CV/Resume, (3) a statement about your experience in supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds, and (4) the contact details for three references, including one for teaching (if a teaching position). Please do not attach additional documents at this time. Supplemental documents may be requested or required of semi-finalists and finalists. For full consideration, apply by November 9, 2026. The position will remain posted until filled . Questions about this position can be directed to the search chair: Dr. Kelly Bruhn, dean of the School of Journalism and Mass Communication, kelly.bruhn@drake.edu   Questions about the application process, working at Drake, spouse/partner support, reasonable accommodations, benefits, or additional information about Drake or Des Moines, Iowa, may be directed to Drake Human Resources at  jobs@drake.edu .   All job offers are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, satisfactory reference checks, and proof of authorization to work in the United States. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Aliber-Hall/EMC-Visiting-Assistant-Professor-of-Actuarial-Science_JR100032": {
      "title": "EMC Visiting Assistant Professor of Actuarial Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nZimpleman College of Business ‌ Department Summary: Drake University's Zimpleman College of Business is a great place to work. The College's faculty possess expertise that combines business and teaching experience that set us apart from other universities. With 38 full-time faculty members and 17 staff members, we are committed to doing the work needed to ensure that the College's students are equipped with the technical skills, business acumen, and experience to prepare them for immediate and lasting success. Our students are given the opportunity to work with actual clients on relevant business matters, bringing in business leaders on a regular basis to work with students, and engaging students in the Drake community. To learn more about the College, visit: https://www.drake.edu/zimpleman/ . Des Moines, Iowa is one of the nation's top headquarters for the finance and insurance industries. Drake has a globally elite actuarial science program located in the most important insurance state in the country.  The state is ranked first in the U.S. in insurance industry output as a percent of GDP.  With over $1 trillion of insurance assets in Iowa and 75 carriers headquartered in Des Moines, there are many opportunities for collaborative research with the industry.  Established in 2015, Iowa’s Global Insurance Accelerator (GIA) is the world's first business accelerator focused on Insurtech and has helped numerous insurance companies from around the world grow and expand.   Drake University offers a Bachelor of Actuarial Science program as either a standalone degree or combined with another Zimpleman College of Business major. Drake also offers two undergraduate minors—one in Risk Management and Insurance and one in Actuarial Science. Learn more at: https://www.drake.edu/actsci/ . Job Summary: We are excited to launch a search for a one-year EMC Visiting Assistant Professor of Actuarial Science. This is a full-time, 9-month appointment starting in August of 2027. In this role, you will enjoy colleagues in a high-performance faculty team focused on teaching and scholarship. The duties of this position include teaching a range of courses supporting the college, including courses related to actuarial science, insurance, and statistics. We are looking for a candidate with strength in research. An existing research record or interest in publishing in actuarial journals is desirable. The search committee is particularly interested in candidates who, through their research, teaching, and/or service, will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in actuarial science, statistics, or closely related field. Preferred Qualifications:   Candidates should demonstrate evidence of teaching effectiveness.   Experience teaching undergraduate actuarial science, insurance, and/or statistics courses.   Actuarial credential such as an ASA, ACAS, FSA, or FCAS. Candidates making progress toward the credential are encouraged to apply.   Demonstrated commitment to Drake University mission and core values.   Publication in peer-reviewed journals. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete the online application and attach (1) a letter of interest, (2) CV/Resume, (3) a statement about your experience in supporting the success of students from diverse backgrounds, and (4) contact information for three references, including one for teaching. Please do not attach additional documents at this time. Supplemental documents may be requested or required of semi-finalists and finalists. For full consideration, apply by December 1, 2026. The position will remain posted until filled. Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about this position can be directed to the search chair: Lendie Follett, Chair and Associate Professor of Business Analytics, lendie.follett@drake.edu.   Questions about the application process, working at Drake, spouse/partner support, reasonable accommodations, benefits, or additional information about Drake or Des Moines, Iowa may be directed to Drake Human Resources at  jobs@drake.edu .   All job offers are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, satisfactory reference checks, and proof of authorization to work in the United States. Salary is competitive with peer schools and will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected candidate.   At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our digital benefits guide:  Benefits Overview | Drake University .   One of our very popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. You can learn about both the tuition waiver policy and tuition exchange programs here: Benefits Overview | Drake University . For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Carnegie-Hall/Adjunct-Instructor--Art-and-Design_JR100039": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Art and Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nCollege of Arts and Sciences JM ‌ Department Summary: The Department of Art and Design offers undergraduate students BA and BFA degrees in Studio Art and Graphic Design and a BA in Art History. Our small department with accomplished faculty provides students with personalized experiences. From classwork to mentoring to internships, we guide students to incorporate their interests and values into their education and career goals. Our courses are designed to encourage curiosity and enhance responsible artistic engagement, involving students in collaborative projects with campus and community organizations and with Drake University’s Anderson Gallery. More information about our department can be found here: https://www.drake.edu/artsci/departments-programs Job Summary: The Department of Art and Design at Drake University is seeking to hire an adjunct instructor who will be responsible for teaching one course covering observational drawing techniques to beginning undergraduate major and non-major students. The successful candidate will have the ability to effectively teach a range of fundamental drawing techniques, lead critical discussion of finished artworks, contribute to the safe use of the drawing studio it’s related equipment and maintaining communication with enrolled students. The course will be conducted in-person twice a week, with each session lasting 2 hours and 20 minutes. Enrollment for the course is capped at 15 students. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelors + 5 years teaching experience or bachelors + industry experience Preferred Qualifications: A MFA, undergraduate teaching experience and a history of sustained artistic practice is preferred. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online. To apply for this position, please include: (1) a letter detailing your experience qualifying you for the position; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a list of three references, including current email addresses and phone numbers; (4) a PDF based or link to a portfolio. If you have any questions about this job posting or the application process, please email emily.newman@drake.edu. A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. All job offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
    },
    "https://jobs.drake.edu/en-US/DrakeCareers/job/Carnegie-Hall/Adjunct-Instructor--Art-and-Design_JR100038": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Art and Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nCollege of Arts and Sciences JM ‌ Department Summary: The Department of Art and Design offers undergraduate students BA and BFA degrees in Studio Art and Graphic Design and a BA in Art History. Our small department with accomplished faculty provides students with personalized experiences. From classwork to mentoring to internships, we guide students to incorporate their interests and values into their education and career goals. Our courses are designed to encourage curiosity and enhance responsible artistic engagement, involving students in collaborative projects with campus and community organizations and with Drake University’s Anderson Gallery. More information about our department can be found here: https://www.drake.edu/artsci/departments-programs Job Summary: Drake University's Department of Art and Design seeks applicants for an Adjunct Instructor position in Graphic Design for the spring semester of 2027. The successful candidate will have the ability to teach Introductory Typography to Art and Design students using current software and computer platforms. This position will teach 1 course. Ability to instruct students in contemporary graphic design workflow processes using current Adobe software on the Apple OS platform. Ability to effectively evaluate and offer critical feedback to students on a range of conceptual, formal, technical and professional subjects. Minimum Qualifications: A MA / MFA, BA / BFA in Graphic Design or related art field and evidence of teaching effectiveness Preferred Qualifications: The successful candidate should have significant practical experience as a graphic design professional, and experience in the use of Adobe CC software. ‌ Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online. To apply for this position, please include: (1) a letter detailing your experience qualifying you for the position; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a list of three references, including current email addresses and phone numbers; (4) a PDF based or link to a portfolio. If you have any questions about this job posting or the application process, please email emily.newman@drake.edu. A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. All job offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. About Drake: Drake University  is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY   At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. Drake University is proud to support an equal opportunity, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming workplace. Learn more about why Drake is an exceptional place to work: An Exceptional Working Environment | Drake University Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (ph: 515.271.3133; email:  jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. At Drake University, we highly value a diverse, inclusive workforce. We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We stand firmly against discrimination including on the basis of race, color, national origin, creed, religion, age, disability, sex, pregnancy, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, genetic information, veteran status, or any characteristic protected by law."
